  "note": "Independent re-judgment against RFC 9494 Sections 4.3 and 4.6 ('The route SHOULD NOT be advertised to any neighbor from which the Long-Lived Graceful Restart Capability has not been received. The exception is described in Section 4.6.') after intervening changes in forward_rs.go, reactor_api_relay.go, reactor_notify.go, and test/plugin/llgr-egress-state-unloaded.ci. In reactorForwardRSSectionResult, adding pre-policy Adj-RIB-Out BMP observation (emitPrePolicyAdjRIBOut), passing &chainSession by pointer, and AIGP revision tracking leave export policy evaluation and LLGR egress filtering unchanged. In buildRelayUpdate, changing src to *relaySource is a pure pointer refactor preserving relayRebuiltMeta, source-llgr-advertised, and source address. In notifyMessageReceiverFrom/notifyOneMessage, RFC 7947 Section 2.1 rs-client update-filtered retention guards cache/AIGP/eventBus with !filtered and preserves routeMeta, msg.Meta, ru.Meta, and SourceReceipt for accepted UPDATEs. In test/plugin/llgr-egress-state-unloaded.ci, only the LLGR config block syntax was updated to short-lived/long-lived family (3c2a055fd9), leaving the source UPDATE hex, peer topology, and NO_EXPORT (FFFFFF01) wire expectation unchanged. All 16 Go test units and all GR/RIB producers are byte-identical.",
